{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEvenPart_add_barOddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEvenPart_add_barOddPart","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L187-L192","doc":"**Reconstruction.**  `f = barEvenPart f + barOddPart f` on the punctured line.\nSo `BarEven f` is exactly `barOddPart f = 0`: the parity filter is the vanishing\nof a well-defined odd component, not a soft numerical criterion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_barOddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_barOddPart","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L184-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barEvenPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barEvenPart","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L181-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOddPart","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L178-L179","doc":"Bar-odd part `(f q − f q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEvenPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEvenPart","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L175-L176","doc":"Bar-even part `(f q + f q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barOdd_forces_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barOdd_forces_zero","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L160-L171","doc":"**Exclusion (`CharZero`).**  Over a characteristic-zero field, a function that\nis both bar-even and bar-odd is identically zero on `q ≠ 0`.  This is the filter:\nthe bar-odd part of a required-bar-even μ-correction must vanish, so the refuted\nbar-mixed projector shift (#2584) is **structurally excluded** — not merely a\nnumerical near-miss. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barOdd_forces_two_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barOdd_forces_two_zero","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L151-L158","doc":"**Common-parity collapse.**  A function that is *both* bar-even and bar-odd\nsatisfies `f q + f q = 0` everywhere on the punctured line.  Over any field: the\neven law gives `f q⁻¹ = f q`, the odd law gives `f q⁻¹ = −f q`, so `f q = −f q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_coloredJones41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_coloredJones41","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L139-L147","doc":"**The figure-8 (`4₁`) colored-Jones tower is bar-even**, for every color\n`N`.  This *packages* the sorry-free `coloredJones41_bar_symmetric`\n(`QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroNewtonLadder`) into the `BarEven` predicate: the muon\nanchor `m_μ = m_e·Vol(4₁)/ℏ_q²` sits on the amphichiral figure-8, whose knot\ninvariant is palindromic.  Any correction *factored through this tower* inherits\nbar-evenness by the closure algebra above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_barOdd_pow_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_barOdd_pow_odd","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**Odd power of a bar-odd generator is bar-odd** (`deltaSign = −1` at odd\nprincipal grading). Together with the previous lemma this is exactly\n`deltaSign = (-1)^(principal grading)`: the Δ_λ chirality sign is the\nbar-involution parity of the principal-grading degree — the SAME `ℤ/2` grading\nthat forces the μ-correction bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barOdd_pow_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_barOdd_pow_even","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L120-L125","doc":"**Even power of a bar-odd generator is bar-even** (`deltaSign = +1` at even\nprincipal grading). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_pow","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L115-L118","doc":"A **bar-odd** function raised to the `n`-th power picks up `(-1)^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L98-L101","doc":"`ℏ = q − q⁻¹` is **bar-odd** (the unbalanced difference). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_bracket2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_bracket2","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L93-L96","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` is **bar-even** (the balanced quantum integer). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_mul_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_mul_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L85-L89","doc":"**bar-even × bar-odd = bar-odd** (a single uncancelled sign flip). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_mul_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_mul_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Product of two **bar-odd** functions is **bar-even** (the two sign flips\ncancel) — this is why `ℏ²`-order corrections can be bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_neg","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L75-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barOdd_add","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_mul","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L67-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_add","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barEven_const","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.BarOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.BarOdd","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`f` is **bar-odd** if it negates under `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.BarEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.BarEven","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L53-L54","doc":"`f` is **bar-even** if invariant under `q ↦ q⁻¹` (on the punctured line). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarParityInvariant.barConj","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarParityInvariant.lean#L50-L51","doc":"The bar-conjugate of `f`: precompose with the bar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}